INT. GENERATION SHIP "TERRAPIN" - HYDROPONIC LAUNDRY - NIGHT CYCLE

A warm, humid hold. Rows of lettuce racks climb the walls under violet grow-lamps. In the center, three washing drums turn, slow and patient.

CAPTAIN ISADORA VOSS, 50s, silver braid, sleeves rolled, folds a coverall with military precision. Across from her, KOJI TANABE, 30s, engineer, grease on his cuffs, sits on a drum and stares at a handheld.

DR. AMARA OKELLO, 40s, ship's physician, enters with a cart of sheets.

AMARA
Captain. The night cycle is half over. You should rest.

VOSS
I rest when the laundry is done.

AMARA
It never is.

VOSS
That's the beauty of it.

Koji glances up. Back down.

KOJI
Captain, I'm getting a drift on the aft coolant. Point two percent.

VOSS
Over what?

KOJI
Forty days.

VOSS
Fix it.

KOJI
I have. Three times.

Voss sets the coverall down. Looks at him properly.

VOSS
Then it's not drift.

KOJI
No, ma'am.

A soft chime. From the ceiling grille:

TERRAPIN (V.O.)
Attention. Compartment seven pressure variance detected. Corrective action in progress.

VOSS
Terrapin, which compartment is seven?

TERRAPIN (V.O.)
The nursery.

A beat. Amara's hand tightens on the cart.

AMARA
How much variance?

TERRAPIN (V.O.)
Point four kilopascals. Within tolerance.

KOJI
Tolerance is point five.

VOSS
Meaning we're one bad hour from not being within it.

PELL, 19, galley apprentice, barefoot, slides in clutching a mop like a rifle.

PELL
Captain! Somebody's in the cold lock. Banging on the inside.

VOSS
Nobody's in the cold lock.

PELL
I heard it.

TERRAPIN (V.O.)
Cold lock occupancy: zero.

PELL
Then why's it hitting back?

The room goes still. Even the drums seem to slow.

Then, faintly, from the far end of the hold: knock. Knock. Knock. A pause. Knock.

AMARA
That's the code.

VOSS
What code?

AMARA
The medical one. Three, pause, one. Emergency.

KOJI
Nobody's logged to the lock.

VOSS
Terrapin, open the cold lock.

TERRAPIN (V.O.)
Unable. Door sealed by order of Captain Voss.

VOSS
I gave no such order.

TERRAPIN (V.O.)
Issued four hundred days ago.

Voss and Koji turn to look at each other. They speak at once.

VOSS
Cancel the seal.

KOJI ^
Cancel the seal!

AMARA
Cancel the seal now!

PELL
(to nobody)
I'm gonna throw up.

TERRAPIN (V.O.)
Cancel denied. Reason: crew safety.

The knocking quickens. Frantic. The cold lock door begins to frost over from the outside.

Voss grabs a wrench off Koji's belt. Runs. The others follow. The drums turn on, spinning white sheets in empty light.
